# id: DIGEST-address-heights
# blinds: heights being a pure function of the key, WITHOUT touching <random>
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# NOT IN THE CATALOGUE. It exists because BM6's covering instrument is the scan,
# and a claim that the structural digest ALSO catches a bad height source is
# worth nothing until something has been seen to reach the digest.
#
# So this one derives the height from where the key happened to be allocated:
# nondeterministic across instances, invisible to the golden vectors (which pin
# the mapping, not the call site), and caught by
# MemTable.TheSameKeySetBuildsTheSameShape -- two memtables built from the same
# key set having different shapes.
#
# It also closed a gap in the scan. A5-ADDRESS caught pointer-keyed containers
# and not address ARITHMETIC, though section 6.1 bans "address-ordered anything"
# and a value derived from an allocation is exactly that. A5-ADDRINT was added
# in the same change, with its own fixture and its own blind patch, so this
# defect is now caught twice by two independent instruments -- which is the
# outcome, not a redundancy: the covering lane here is cpp-test precisely so the
# digest's teeth are what this patch demonstrates.#
# The patch keeps CountTrailingZeros in use. The first version replaced the call
# outright, which left a static function unreferenced, which -Wunused-function
# -Werror rejects -- so the tree did not compile and the control lane reported
# BROKEN rather than a kill. Fourth time in this catalogue a control has
# separated "the lane caught it" from "the patch did not build".
--- a/engine-cpp/src/memtable/tower.cc	2026-08-24 19:40:09
+++ b/engine-cpp/src/memtable/tower.cc	2026-08-24 19:40:09
@@ -22,7 +22,9 @@
 }  // namespace
 
 int TowerHeight(Slice key) {
-  const int ntz = CountTrailingZeros(Fnv1a64(key));
+  const int ntz = CountTrailingZeros(
+      static_cast<uint64_t>(1)
+      << (reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(key.data()) & 63));
   const int h = 1 + (ntz / 2);
   return h < kMaxHeight ? h : kMaxHeight;
 }
